    "title": "LESSON 41: ONE ROOT, SIX VERBS",
    "header_color": "yellow",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Now watch the machine run whole.",
          "Take -zaa, to bear a child:",
          "",
          "   kuzaa      to give birth",
          "   kuzaliwa   to BE born (passive)",
          "   kuzalisha  to produce (causative)",
          "   kuzaliana  to breed, multiply",
          "              (reciprocal)",
          "",
          "   Nilizaliwa Dodoma.",
          "   I was born in Dodoma.",
          "",
          "Hear the family:                   Press 1"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Kuzaa. Kuzaliwa. Kuzalisha. Nilizaliwa Dodoma."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Or -funga, to close (tier 3's verb):",
          "",
          "   kufunga    to close, tie",
          "   kufungwa   to be shut (by someone)",
          "   kufungika  to be closeable / stuck",
          "   kufungia   to lock away FOR/ON",
          "   kufungana  to be bound together",
          "",
          "Hear the chain:                    Press 1",
          "",
          "Beads even stack: kufungULIWA — to",
          "be unlocked — carries reversal AND",
          "passive at once. You no longer",
          "memorise such verbs; you READ them,",
          "bead by bead, like arithmetic."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Kufunga. Kufungwa. Kufungika. Kufungia. Kufunguliwa."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "042",
    "trigger_word": "jinamizi",
    "trigger_card_number": 1,
    "title": "LESSON 42: COMPOUND TENSES",
    "header_color": "red",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "The hours of sleep need layered",
          "time: was-doing, had-done. Swahili",
          "builds them with kuwa as a carrier",
          "verb plus a second bead:",
          "",
          "   Nilikuwa nikisoma.",
          "   I was reading. (-li- + -ki-)",
          "",
          "   Watoto walikuwa wamelala.",
          "   The children had lain down —",
          "   were asleep. (-li- + -me-)",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Nilikuwa nikisoma. Watoto walikuwa wamelala."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "The carrier takes any tense; the",
          "second verb holds the aspect:",
          "",
          "   Nitakuwa nimemaliza kesho.",
          "   I will have finished by tomorrow.",
          "",
          "   Alikuwa akifanya kazi usiku.",
          "   She used to work nights.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "Two verbs, one thought: kuwa sets",
          "the stage clock, the partner verb",
          "acts on it. English needed 'will",
          "have been' — Swahili needs only",
          "the beads you already own."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Nitakuwa nimemaliza kesho. Alikuwa akifanya kazi usiku."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
]
